  <h2>What this is — and what it isn't</h2>
  <ul class="tft-caveats">
    <li>A sample, not a census: 5 independent stratified replicates of NA ranked players with 20+ ranked games in Set 18. It is not all ranked players.</li>
    <li>The 20+ games filter skews tiers — Bronze is under-sampled, Gold and Platinum over-sampled against League of Graphs — corrected by stratification weights. The error bars on the chart are the spread across the 5 replicates (sampling noise only).</li>
    <li>The field behind this chart counts top-4 finishes, not 1st-place finishes: the unweighted pooled median is 50.0% and the games-weighted mean is 50.35%, where 1st-place finishes would average 12.5%. A spot-check of one sampled Master player gave a 60.0% top-4 rate against a 30.0% 1st-place rate over their last 30 ranked matches.</li>
    <li>Snapshot dated Nov. 23, 2026, patch 18.7, Set 18 only. Never averaged across sets.</li>
  </ul>

